# Which ref of this plugin each Discourse core version should check out.
#
# Format: `<core version constraint>: <plugin git ref>`, lowest matching
# entry wins. Parsed by `Discourse.find_compatible_resource`
# (core `lib/version_compatibility.rb`) and applied at image build time by
# `rake plugin:pull_compatible_all`, which our `web-only.yml` build runs via
# the `plugin_compatibility` hook. Cores not matched here get the default
# branch.
#
# Why there is an entry at all: `web-only.yml` clones this repo with no ref,
# so every forum we run loads whatever is on `main` — and we only test
# against dev's core. Dev is on calendar versioning (`2026.8.0-latest.1`)
# while support.primero.org is still on `3.6.0.beta3-latest`, so one commit
# has to satisfy both. This entry stops that being true by accident.
#
# bc2e5d1 is the last commit with `.hbs` connectors, which is what
# support.primero.org is verifiably running today. Cores older than the
# calendar-version era stay on it; dev gets the `.gjs` conversion, which
# `2026.8.0-latest` requires.
#
# ⚠️ This pins the pre-2026.7 forums to bc2e5d1 for good: later plugin
# fixes will NOT reach them until this ref is bumped. Bump it (or delete the
# entry) when support.primero.org's core is upgraded.
< 2026.7.0: bc2e5d1
